      "value": "@{5e44a1bd0c91c2477a8b8acb|full_name}: let me go over them from point to point:\n- \"default base layer\" as well as my own\n- on this avatar its on disable, its there when its enabled as well as sdk2 avatars\n- my controller does use \"proxy_stand_still\" whenever fbt is not moving.\n- additive layer using default (meaning i didnt set anything there)\n- world in this case is sdk3, seen that issue additionally in void club and black cat to name some, the latter is sdk2 i think?\n- if you mean to use a different ik controller then no.\n- physical rotation to that direction causes it as well.\nBehaviour is seen as mentioned on sdk3 and sdk2 avatars - therefore i assume that it is not within sdk3 avatars locomotion/additive layer\nPS: in black cat it the angle is left(ish) in the world. Let me quickly paint where you will find it most easily. You go into the big room on the mirror on the left, in case you want to check it out for yourself. Have your camera pointing at you and do slowly rotate.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
